 "background": "One of the oldest and most covered songs in the repertoire. A falcon drinking from the Vardar is asked whether he has seen a hero pass with nine deadly wounds, all from bullets, and a tenth from a knife. Between the lines the refrain keeps singing to Jane. *Бело грло* (\"white throat\") means a person with a beautiful singing voice. Qwen reads the knife wound as the one that lands hardest, since a bullet is honourable and a blade is not (an interpretation, unchecked).",
